    "body": "A detail that I haven't seen covered elsewhere, but thankfully it's consistent between browsers: POST navigations to the same URL append a new entry, rather than replace the current entry.\r\n\r\nGET form submissions appear to behave like link clicks (phew). Navigations _from_ a page that loaded via a form submission don't appear to behave in any special way (also phew).\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Tests</summary>\r\n\r\nTest:\r\n\r\n1. https://iframe-session-history.glitch.me/\r\n1. Click \"Navigate via POST to /\" - add or replace?\r\n1. Click \"Navigate via POST to /\" - add or replace?\r\n\r\nChrome, Firefox, Safari: add add\r\n\r\nTest:\r\n\r\n1. https://iframe-session-history.glitch.me/?\r\n1. Click \"Navigate via form GET to /\" - add or replace?\r\n\r\nChrome, Firefox, Safari: Replace\r\n\r\nTest:\r\n\r\n1. https://iframe-session-history.glitch.me/\r\n1. Click \"Navigate via POST\"\r\n1. Click \"Navigate to current URL\" - add or replace?\r\n\r\nChrome, Firefox, Safari: Replace\r\n\r\n</details>",
